(order of integration.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Identify given region R from integration limits:) Tj
T*
(Inner integral: y runs from y = x to y = 1.) Tj
T*
(Outer integral: x runs from x = 0 to x = 1.) Tj
T*
(Region R is the triangle bounded by the line y = x, the horizontal line y = 1, and the) Tj
T*
(y-axis \(x = 0\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Reverse order to integrate with respect to x first, then y:) Tj
T*
(For a fixed horizontal slice y, x varies from x = 0 \(y-axis\) to x = y \(the boundary) Tj
T*
(line\).) Tj
T*
(y varies along the full vertical height of the region from y = 0 to y = 1.) Tj
T*
(Transformed Integral: I = int_{y=0}^1 [ int_{x=0}^y e^{y^2} dx ] dy.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Evaluate inner integral with respect to x \(treating e^{y^2} as) Tj
T*
(constant\):) Tj
T*
(int_0^y e^{y^2} dx = e^{y^2} * [ x ]_0^y = y * e^{y^2}.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Evaluate outer integral with respect to y:) Tj
T*
(I = int_0^1 y * e^{y^2} dy.) Tj
T*
(Let u = y^2 => du = 2y dy => y dy = du / 2.) Tj
T*
(When y = 0, u = 0; when y = 1, u = 1.) Tj
T*
(I = \(1 / 2\) * int_0^1 e^u du = \(1 / 2\) * [ e^u ]_0^1 = \(1 / 2\) * \(e^1 - e^0\) = \(e - 1\) /) Tj
T*
(2.) Tj
