(Problem: Evaluate iint_R sqrt\(a^2 - x^2 - y^2\) dx dy over the positive first quadrant of) Tj
T*
(the circle x^2 + y^2 <= a^2.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Convert to polar coordinates: x = r*cos\(theta\), y = r*sin\(theta\), dx dy) Tj
T*
(= r dr d\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(Integrand: sqrt\(a^2 - \(x^2 + y^2\)\) = sqrt\(a^2 - r^2\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Determine limits for the first quadrant of circle of radius a:) Tj
T*
(r runs from r = 0 to r = a.) Tj
T*
(theta runs from theta = 0 to theta = pi/2.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Set up and evaluate iterated integral:) Tj
T*
(I = int_{theta=0}^{pi/2} [ int_{r=0}^a sqrt\(a^2 - r^2\) * r dr ] d\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(Inner Integral: Let u = a^2 - r^2 => du = -2r dr => r dr = -du / 2.) Tj
T*
(When r = 0, u = a^2; when r = a, u = 0.) Tj
T*
(int_{a^2}^0 sqrt\(u\) * \(-du / 2\) = \(1 / 2\) * int_0^{a^2} u^{1/2} du = \(1 / 2\) * [ \(2/3\) *) Tj
T*
(u^{3/2} ]_0^{a^2}) Tj
T*
(= \(1 / 3\) * \(a^2\)^{3/2} = a^3 / 3.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Outer Integral:) Tj
T*
(I = int_0^{pi/2} [ a^3 / 3 ] d\(theta\) = \(a^3 / 3\) * [ theta ]_0^{pi/2} = \(a^3 / 3\) * \(pi) Tj
T*
(/ 2\) = pi * a^3 / 6.) Tj
T*
(Final Answer: Integral value = pi * a^3 / 6.) Tj
T*
