(Problem: Evaluate the volume of a sphere of radius R using spherical polar coordinates.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Coordinate transformation: x = rho*sin\(phi\)*cos\(theta\), y =) Tj
T*
(rho*sin\(phi\)*sin\(theta\), z = rho*cos\(phi\).) Tj
T*
(Jacobian volume element: dV = rho^2 * sin\(phi\) d\(rho\) d\(phi\) d\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Define spherical limits for full sphere:) Tj
T*
(Radial distance rho: 0 to R.) Tj
T*
(Colatitude \(polar angle\) phi: 0 to pi.) Tj
T*
(Azimuthal angle theta: 0 to 2*pi.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Set up and separate independent triple integral:) Tj
T*
(Volume V = int_0^{2*pi} d\(theta\) * int_0^pi sin\(phi\) d\(phi\) * int_0^R rho^2 d\(rho\).) Tj
T*
(Integral 1: int_0^{2*pi} d\(theta\) = 2*pi.) Tj
T*
(Integral 2: int_0^pi sin\(phi\) d\(phi\) = [ -cos\(phi\) ]_0^pi = -cos\(pi\) - \(-cos\(0\)\) = -\(-1\)) Tj
T*
(+ 1 = 2.) Tj
T*
(Integral 3: int_0^R rho^2 d\(rho\) = [ rho^3 / 3 ]_0^R = R^3 / 3.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Multiply results:) Tj
T*
(V = \(2*pi\) * \(2\) * \(R^3 / 3\) = \(4/3\) * pi * R^3. \(Exact Standard Formula Proven\).) Tj
T*
